{
 "_about": "Hand-curated rows for algid (scripts/algid/build_algid.py). Every section cites its document; rows that a registry already defines are generated from the captured registry files instead. A second-agent review (O-9) of this file is recorded in the PR that changes it.",
 "attributes": "[family_label, primitive, standard, status, parameter_set, nist_category, construction, quantum, key_size, components]",
 "status_rule": "status of every registry row (TLS groups and signature schemes, SSH KEX, IKEv2 type 4, PKIX) comes from one rule on its Reference and Description columns, first match wins: 'obsolete' (any case) in either -> obsolete; a published RFC '[RFC NNNN]' -> standard, and `standard` names it; an RFC-to-be 'RFC-ietf-*' (approved, no RFC number yet) -> draft; an Internet-Draft 'draft-*' -> draft; anything else -> standard. RFC-to-be is draft by coordinator decision (2026-11-12): no credit for text that is not published, and CB-16 grants credit from this field. Curated rows state their status here. parameter_set is a FIPS 203/204/205 set (or the FN-DSA set of the forthcoming FIPS 206); pre-standard and obsolete identities never carry one (FIPS 203 App. C and FIPS 204 App. D list how round-3 Kyber/Dilithium differ). components are canonical algid names (rows of this table); a composite's hash and padding stay in its name.",
